# Copy to demo/.env and fill in. `demo/.env` is gitignored; this file is not, so
# never put a real value here.
#
#   cp demo/.env.example demo/.env
#
# This is the demo's own config, separate from the repo root's `.env`. The two
# hold API keys for two different Hookdeck projects and must not be crossed:
# `reset.sh` deletes connections and sets every OPENED issue to IGNORED in
# whichever project it is given, and the root `.env` points at the project the
# live test suite depends on. Nothing falls back from one file to the other.
#
# An exported environment variable wins over anything set here, which is what
# makes a one-off override work:
#
#   N8N_URL=http://localhost:5679 ./demo/reset.sh

# API key for the Hookdeck project the demo runs in, from Project Settings ->
# Secrets. Use a throwaway project - never one carrying live traffic.
#
# Named DEMO rather than the bare HOOKDECK_API_KEY on purpose: the Hookdeck CLI
# reads HOOKDECK_API_KEY from the environment, so a shell that has one exported
# for CLI use would silently redirect this script at that project instead.
HOOKDECK_DEMO_API_KEY=

# No n8n API key here on purpose. `reset.sh` needs to unpublish and republish a
# workflow - that is what forces Hookdeck to hand out a fresh connection id, and
# a fresh connection id is the only thing that resets issue aggregation
# (measured: dismissing an issue does not, see README). The obvious way to do
# that is the n8n Public API, but:
#
#   "The n8n API isn't available during the free trial. Please upgrade to
#    access this feature."   - https://docs.n8n.io/connect/n8n-api/authentication
#
# So the instance MCP server (Settings -> Instance-level MCP) is the route
# instead. Which credential the script uses for it is still open - see
# README.md, "Reaching n8n".

# Base URL of the n8n instance. Defaults to http://localhost:5678 when unset; a
# trailing slash is trimmed. For n8n Cloud this is the instance URL:
#
#   N8N_URL=https://your-instance.app.n8n.cloud
#
# Hookdeck delivers over the public internet. A publicly reachable n8n - Cloud,
# or self-hosted with WEBHOOK_URL set - lets the trigger provision an HTTP
# destination and takes the Hookdeck CLI out of the demo entirely, so run
# `reset.sh --no-listen`. A localhost n8n needs `hookdeck listen`, which is what
# the script starts by default.
N8N_URL=
